OL,3,GNEWSACaretaker restores school's
OL,4,Ahistoric clock
OL,5,
OL,6,FFor most people work is quite literally
OL,7,Fthe last place they would choose to
OL,8,Fspend their annual leave - but that's
OL,9,Fexactly where one North Yorkshire
OL,10,Fcaretaker spent his two weeks off.
OL,12,FThe clock in Ripon Grammar School's
OL,13,Fstriking clock tower, which dates back
OL,14,Fto 1889, is not believed to have worked
OL,15,Fproperly for decades.
OL,17,FThat was until 32-year-old Matthew
OL,18,FBuller became the school's caretaker
OL,19,Flast October and took it upon himself
OL,20,Fto restore the 19th Century timepiece.
OL,23,APub: 23-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
